  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Volunteers can see room crowding, and the reception map can show several equally acceptable routes.\", \"decision\": \"How should crowded rooms influence suggested routes?\", \"goal\": \"Help visitors find a satisfying route through the museum while keeping reception and volunteers manageable.\", \"problem\": \"A volunteer-run local museum wants to make a weekend visit easier to navigate. It has a modest collection, printed guides, a reception table, flexible volunteer positions, and several rooms that can remain open independently. The decisions concern interpretation and visitor organization, not conservation rules or safety policy.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nRoom volunteers report crowding before reception suggests a route to arriving visitors. Initial guidance reflects current room use.\nRoom volunteers offer route changes directly to visitors while reception keeps the map available. Advice follows people already moving through the museum.\nReception sends a small group along a route and then asks room volunteers whether the next group should follow it. Guidance is adjusted after observing each group’s effect."
    }
  ],
